# Line endings, declared rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default and rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. Harmless for a file nobody reads back; NOT harmless for one this
# software writes to and asserts about. On 3 September 2026, the first time
# this branch was checked out on Windows, `test_the_lf_file_stays_lf` failed
# before a line of code ran -- git had already converted `rate_plans.yaml` on
# the way to disk.
#
# The test was right and the repository was silent. This is the repository
# saying what it needs.
* text=auto

# Config this app edits and writes back. The editor preserves LF; checkout
# must not undo that.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Windows entry points, which keep CRLF to be safe in every shell.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
